x ----------CMSC 132-2 ISA DEMO PROGRAM----------
x This program executes a countdown loop from a user-defined
x starting integer down to a user-defined target integer.

x ----------------- User Inputs ---------------------------
x Step 1: Read the starting value from the user into R1
SCAN R1, M:Enter-the-starting-countdown-integer:

x Step 2: Read the target limit value into R2 (e.g., 0)
SCAN R2, M:Enter-the-target-limit-integer:

x ----------------- Block Definitions ---------------------
x Step 3: Define B1 to mark the start of the loop body
CB B1

x ----------------- Main Execution Loop -------------------
x Step 4: Print the current counter value
PRNT R1, M:Current-count:-below-target

x Step 5: Subtract 1 from R1 to decrement the counter
SUB R1, 1

x ----------------- Conditional Comparison ----------------
x Step 6: Load R1 into the Jump Register (JR) to prepare
MOV JR, R1

x Step 7: Compare R1 (inside JR) against our target R2
CMP R2

x Step 8: If the counter R1 is still greater than or equal
x to the target R2 (meaning JR >= 0), branch back to loop start
JGE B1

x ----------------- Exit Sequence -------------------------
x Step 9: Program finished loop. Print success message.
PRNT R1, M:Countdown-finished!-_Goodbye.

x Step 10: Terminate the program
EOP
